task: raft-store-snapshot
agent: fable-persist
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/raft-store-snapshot
worktree: ../okay-wt-rss

why: stage 2c of persist-raft — stage 2b gave the core compaction
  and InstallSnapshot with the bytes the ENGINE's, and RaftStore is
  the engine that has none yet: a RaftStore cluster cannot compact,
  and a node that starts late replays the whole log for ever.

what: RaftStore.snapshot(): the local store's FULL history (every
  topic, every partition, every record with its offset) as one CBOR
  image at the last applied index, handed to Node.compact — refused
  when any partition's `begin` is past 0 (retention or local
  compaction has dropped history the image would need, and offsets
  must survive a restore). Restore: the image's records past the
  local store's own `end` are appended in offset order (the local
  store holds a prefix of the same history, by construction), and
  entries at or before the image's index are skipped when the core
  re-applies from the snapshot's edge; a gap between the local `end`
  and the image's next offset is named loudly and refused, never
  papered over. Optional auto-snapshot every N applied entries.
  Live test: two stores commit and snapshot, a third starts late
  and reads the same records at the same offsets.
